---
import "@styles/global.module.css";
import Header from "@components/header.astro";
import Footer from "@components/footer.astro";
import Meta from "@components/meta.astro";
import Cursor from "@components/cursor.astro";
import Scripts from "@components/scripts.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <Meta name="Why I won't fix my My Summer Car mods" description="Explaining that these mods are unsupported, and it's up to the user to downgrade MSCLoader or fix the mods themself." />
        <Scripts />
        <Cursor />
    </head>

    <body>
        <canvas id="background"></canvas>
        <!-- God damnit, I'm forced to use inline styles because Astro is stupid -->
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;">
            <Header />
            <main>
                <h1>Why I won't fix my My Summer Car mods</h1>
                
                <p><i>sigh</i> Well, one small post about this wasn't enough, so I have to make another bigger one.</p>

                <p style="font-size: 36px;"><strong>These mods are simply no longer supported. They have been for over 8 months, since 1/31/24. It's surprising they kept working.</strong></p>

                <p>One possible solution is to use FreeMSCLoader.It has a correctly tagged build, maintains compatibility with MSCLoader, mods with legitimacy checks, and older mods. It's dangerous to use HTTP software in production.Transferring tokens to an MSCLoader account over HTTP is risky; hackers could access your account and replace mods with malware.</p>

                <p>I won't update the mods. I really meant it when I said these mods aren't supported.They're open source, so feel free to fork and release on NexusMods under a different name.If someone contacts me with copyright concerns, I'll check your mod to see if it follows the open source license.If it does, I'll tell them and explain that everything's fine. Credit is appreciated but not needed. And probably not preferred.</p>

                <p><a href="https://social.mldchan.dev/notes/a3ytiwehnhgf010z">This post</a> summarizes the current state of MSCLoader</p>

                <p>And if you missed it, <a href="https://social.mldchan.dev/notes/a1tsf5xe9kiu00r2">here's approximately why I left the modding community</a>. (There are content warnings including gore under that link, although the post itself has a CW)</p>

                <p>I hope this summarizes the state of this and I won't have to respond to another thing about this again.</p>
            </main>
            <Footer />
        </div>
        <script is:inline defer src="/scripts/background.js"></script>
    </body>
</html>
